course: dictionary
lesson: 11841
title: Feeling bliss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bliss is a noun for perfect happiness and calm joy. It is the feeling of being completely content, like sinking into a warm bath after a long day. «This bath is bliss!» means the bath gives the speaker great pleasure.
explain: Read the words around bliss to find its meaning. «She lay in the hammock, eyes closed, listening to the waves. Pure bliss.» The calm, relaxed words around it show that bliss is peaceful happiness, not wild excitement.
explain: Bliss has no plural, so you never write «blisses» for the feeling. Writers also use bliss in set phrases: «sheer bliss», «wedded bliss», and «ignorance is bliss», which means it can feel easier not to know something bad.
fact: Bliss means perfect happiness and calm joy.
fact: «Bliss» can also mean something that gives you great pleasure, as in «This bath is bliss!»
fact: Bliss is a noun with no plural, so you never write «blisses» for the feeling.
fact: In Christian writing, bliss can mean the perfect happiness of heaven that Christians believe God gives.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole feels bliss on his first day on the river.
exercise: «After the cold swim, the hot drink was pure bliss.» What does bliss mean here? | A cold, wet shiver | *Perfect, calm happiness and pleasure | A loud and angry noise | A sharp pain in the leg
exercise: «The sun was warm, the grass was soft, and Sam felt sheer bliss.» What is Sam feeling? | *Complete happiness and calm | A fast, noisy race | A sharp pain | A long, tiring walk
exercise: Which phrase means it can feel easier not to know something bad? | Bliss is a sort of cake | Wedded bliss | *Ignorance is bliss | Count to ten first
exercise: Which sentence uses bliss correctly? | I felt a blisses in the sun | *I felt bliss in the sun | I felt blisses in the sun | I felt many bliss in the suns
test: «Ben sank into the warm bath and sighed, “This is bliss!”» What does bliss mean here? | A rainy day | *Great pleasure and happiness | A loud argument | A sharp pain
test: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole feels bliss on his first day on the river. What does this tell you about Mole? | He is angry and cross | He is very tired and hungry | *He feels perfectly happy and calm | He is scared of the water
exam: «Nell had sheer bliss curled up with her book by the fire.» What does sheer bliss suggest about Nell? | *She is completely happy and relaxed | She is angry with her book | She is about to be sick | She is cold and bored
